flowchart TD
    accTitle: The Orchard content lifecycle
    accDescr: Scheduled discovery, scheduled currency inspection, and content requests feed a shared proposal queue. Gate 1 authorizes authoring. Failed review returns work for correction. Gate 2 binds approval to an exact artifact. Publication, platform release, site deployment, and live verification are separate steps that can each hold until their evidence is complete.

    subgraph INTAKE["Three intake paths, one proposal queue"]
        discovery["Discovery: monthly on the 1st"] --> queue["Shared proposal queue"]
        currency["Currency: monthly on the 15th"] --> queue
        request["Labeled content request"] --> queue
    end

    queue --> gate1{"Gate 1: approve the proposal?"}
    gate1 -->|no| stop1["No authoring authority"]
    gate1 -->|yes| tracker["Link the work item"]
    tracker --> author["Research and author the artifact"]
    author --> review{"Factual and assessment review pass?"}
    review -->|no| rework["Correct the draft with review findings"]
    rework --> author
    review -->|yes| gate2{"Gate 2: approve this exact artifact?"}
    gate2 -->|no| rework
    gate2 -->|yes| pull["Open a content pull request"]
    pull --> merge["Validate and merge into canonical content"]
    merge --> release["Release the platform content package"]
    release --> deploy["Update the learner site package pin"]
    deploy --> verify["Verify the lesson is live"]

    hold["Any failed check holds the item with its reason"]
    review -.-> hold
    merge -.-> hold
    release -.-> hold
    verify -.-> hold
